A child profile that sets its parent's only write back to read grants none.
Codex applies the parent and then the child, rule by rule, so what the child
says at a path is what holds there, and a scan reading the parent's grant on
its own would report a write the agent does not have.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
default_permissions = "ours"

[permissions.base.filesystem]
"/srv" = "write"

[permissions.ours]
extends = "base"

[permissions.ours.filesystem]
"/srv" = "read"
